cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RePlanWeaver, please cite this repository."
title: "RePlanWeaver: Mid-Course Review and Delta-Replan for Multi-Agent Task Graphs"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-12
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Zhengming (正明)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/chenhz01/replanweaver"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A zero-dependency Python engine that checks intermediate agent outputs against
  machine-verifiable expectation contracts, propagates deviations along the task
  dependency graph, replans only the affected subtree, caps replanning with a
  hard budget, and distills failures into reusable priors.
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - replanning
  - verification
  - expectation contract
  - failure taxonomy
